For a response with a content coding, Ladybird reports an unknown length
in every XMLHttpRequest progress event. Chromium does the same:
URLRequestJob only takes the expected content size from Content-Length
when the body isn’t filtered by a decoding SourceStream, so Blink’s
XMLHttpRequest::DispatchProgressEvent() gets no expected length for it.
WebKit’s XMLHttpRequest::didReceiveData() instead reports Content-Length
until the received length passes it, and Gecko reports the channel’s
encoded progress against Content-Length.
